          "field": "description",
          "page_id": "page-49e2e05a7ef3a1264178b628",
          "qa_findings": [],
          "review_status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "segment_id": "seg-74f6f5f7a0e715160cb97ece",
          "segment_index": 13,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-74f6f5f7a0e715160cb97ece",
          "source_text_sha256": "efb0988b605b3bf6fca6ae79071d69cd35710a14359d7a64e5ee1710ca308150",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness observes each night (without specifying for how long) starting at 9:45 PM a bright point, soon followed by a second, less bright one. These points move slowly together and disappear hidden by the landscape. The long and repeated observation of bright points in the sky obviously suggests a mundane astronomical phenomenon: stars or planets. A check with a sky map indicates Venus and Jupiter exactly in the observation axis of the witness. It is regrettable that the witness, despite being of a high level of university study, did not independently think of an astronomical phenomenon; he was clearly too influenced by TV shows on the topic of UFOs. The GEIPAN classifies this case A: observation of Venus and Jupiter.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "5afe1661ae3ee01d37d871386a862b0a92dbe6268f257a308eb39347fe55bc53"
        }
      ],
